(P/'noira-dental-source-audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)+'\n')
(P/'noira-dental-source-audit.md').write_text('# Priority: Noira dental stops misread as retroflex\n\nThe original printed dental **d̪/t̪** were stored as **ɖ/ʈ**, producing compiled **ḍ/ṭ**. This is an ingestion reading error, not evidence for a historical sound change. Physical p. 52 (printed p. 46), item 91 milk, shows dental stops in the Hindi, Gujarati, Marathi and relevant Bhil rows; genuine retroflex stops occur separately in the non-Indo-Aryan comparison rows.\n\nVerified physical pages: 34, 42, 52, 58, 65, 66; printed pages: 28, 36, 46, 52, 59, 60. These support the tooth, star, milk, night, simple red, and seven etymology links. Exact IDs and source cells are in `noira-dental-verified-cells.json`.\n\nNo lexical-source, compiled-form or identity data was changed. A source correction must follow SOURCE_INGESTION_CHECKLIST.md and reconcile durable IDs, existing links and affected artifacts. Other glyphs/pages/sources remain unverified; do not apply a global replacement.\n\nPDF SHA-256: '+report['pdfSha256']+'\n\nEtymology records linked from verified readings: '+str(len(acc))+'\n')
